.TH ZERODDS-AMQP-BRIDGED.YAML 5 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-amqp-bridged.yaml \- configuration file for zerodds-amqp-bridged(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/zerodds/amqp-bridged.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
YAML document describing how the AMQP 1.0 bridge daemon maps DDS topics onto
AMQP addresses. The schema is the one of
.IR zerodds-amqp-bridge-daemon-1.0 " \(sc3;"
the reader is
.I DaemonConfig::from_config
in
.IR crates/amqp-endpoint/src/bridge_daemon.rs .
.PP
Top-level keys:
.BR domain ", " log_level ", " amqp ", " acl ", " metrics ", " topics .
.PP
An unknown top-level key is
.I not
a parse error. The daemon logs a WARN line on stderr naming the key, then
starts; under
.B \-\-check\-config
it is an error. An unknown key inside a known section, or a value of the
wrong type, stops the start with file and line.
.PP
.BI ${VAR} " and " ${VAR:-default}
are substituted from the environment before the document is parsed, so the
broker password belongs in the environment, not in the file.
.SH KEYS
.SS Top level
.TP
.B domain
Integer DDS domain ID. Default
.IR 0 .
.TP
.B log_level
.IR trace " | " debug " | " info " | " warn " | " error .
.SS amqp
.TP
.B broker_url
.IR amqp:// " or " amqps://
URL of the broker, e.g.
.IR "amqp://localhost:5672" ;
ports 5672 and 5671 by default.
.I amqps://
needs
.B tls
enabled, and the other way round.
.TP
.B container_id
AMQP container identifier of this daemon; it also seeds the GUID prefix of
the daemon's DDS participant, so two daemons need two ids.
.TP
.B channel_max
Highest channel number the daemon offers in
.IR Open .
.TP
.B max_frame_size
Largest frame the daemon accepts, in bytes, at least 512; a larger message
travels as a multi-frame transfer.
.TP
.B idle_time_out_ms
Idle timeout in milliseconds, sent in
.IR Open ;
0 announces none. The daemon sends a heartbeat at half the broker's.
.TP
.B hostname
AMQP
.I Open
hostname (virtual host); the broker host when empty.
.TP
.B sasl
Sub-map with
.B mechanism
.RI ( PLAIN " | " SCRAM-SHA-256 " | " EXTERNAL " | " ANONYMOUS " | " XOAUTH2 )
and the
.BR username " / " password
pair the mechanism needs (for XOAUTH2 the password is the bearer token).
PLAIN without TLS and ANONYMOUS are refused towards a broker that is not on
the loopback interface. The broker must offer the configured mechanism.
.TP
.B tls
Sub-map with
.B enabled
(boolean),
.B ca_file
(required: the trust anchor for the broker certificate), the client material
.BR cert_file " / " key_file
(EXTERNAL's identity),
.B verify_hostname
(only
.IR true )
and
.B alpn
(only
.IR [amqp] ).
.TP
.B reconnect
Sub-map with
.BR initial_delay_ms ", " max_delay_ms " and " factor
of the exponential back-off after a lost connection.
.SS acl
.TP
.B default_deny
Boolean: a topic no rule names is closed.
.TP
.B rules
List of maps with
.BR topic ", " read " and " write :
the SASL subjects allowed DDS \(-> AMQP and AMQP \(-> DDS;
.I *
allows every subject.
.SS metrics
.TP
.B enabled
Boolean. Turns on the admin endpoint serving
.IR /metrics ", " /catalog " and " /healthz .
.TP
.B listen
Admin listen address. Default
.IR "127.0.0.1:9094"
when
.B enabled
is true; each bridge daemon has its own port, so several run on one
host without a collision.
.TP
.B path
Only
.IR /metrics .
.SS topics (list)
.TP
.B dds_name
DDS topic name.
.TP
.B dds_type
DDS type name; default the topic name.
.TP
.B keyed
Boolean: the type has key fields (entity kind WithKey). Default
.IR false .
.TP
.B amqp_address
AMQP node address, e.g.
.IR "/queues/orders.events" .
.TP
.B direction
.IR in " | " out " | " bidir .
.I in
carries broker messages into DDS (a receiver link and a DataWriter),
.I out
carries DDS samples to the broker (a DataReader and a sender link),
.I bidir
both. Default
.IR bidir .
.TP
.B sender
Sub-map with
.B settled
(send settled, at-most-once),
.B durable
(terminus durability 0, 1, 2),
.B snd_settle_mode
(0, 1, 2) and
.B rcv_settle_mode
(0, 1).
.TP
.B receiver
Sub-map with
.BR credit ,
the link credit the daemon grants.
.TP
.B qos
Sub-map with
.B reliability
.RI ( reliable " | " best_effort ;
best effort sends settled),
.B durability
.RI ( volatile " | " transient_local " | " transient " | " persistent ;
anything but volatile sends durable messages) and
.B history
with
.B kind
.RI ( keep_last " | " keep_all )
and a
.B depth
for keep_last: how many samples of a sender wait while the broker grants no
credit.
.SH EXAMPLES
See
.IR /usr/share/zerodds/configs/amqp-bridged.yaml.example .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-amqp-bridged (1).
